A||||5||RossT||truck wiper problem||||1||
Z||000000||RossT||11-10-2000||03:15 AM||||I have a 1985 full size chevy 4x4 truck.  Everytime I turn the ignition switch with the key to the start position, the wipers will take 3 swipes then stop.  The wipers work fine otherwise. Would this be in the wiper switch, ignition switch,or elsewhere.  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||11-10-2000||12:20 PM||||It sounds more like a problem with a relay than the actual switch.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||11-11-2000||01:14 PM||||Some 88 Fieros had a similiar problem.  I don't know if anyone ever found out what was the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||11-13-2000||09:26 PM||||That's right, some 88's had the "mysterious wiper" problem.  I believe it was linked to the pulse module.  If you look in any fiero equipped with this option, you will find it to the left (I think) of the steering column while looking up at it.  It looks just like a little 2 x 2 inch heat sink.  Being your truck an 85, I would think that the same or a similar unit could be on yours.  hope this helps!<P>------------------<BR>"The fish who keeps on swimming is the first to chill upstream"||||reg||1
Z||000004||wkayl||11-13-2000||09:29 PM||||Just park it in an irrigation ditch and get a new one (see "My New Truck" link).||||reg||1
Z||000005||RossT||11-20-2000||11:15 PM||||Found the problem,   Fierojoe was on target!!<BR>The wiper delay module (relay) was the culpret!!!<P>Thanks<P>as a side note, you can take the module out, and conect the two ends and the wipers will<BR>work, but you will not have the delay function.  <p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 11-20-2000).]||||reg||1
